        "text_tNNyqd": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Businesses must take a variety of measures to ensure the safety of their customers and employees. In many cases, they’re obligated by OSHA to identify and eliminate potential hazards; in other situations, it makes sense to offer people a heads-up about potentially risky obstacles or circumstances to help them have a positive experience. There are many ways to do this, with different requirements depending on the particular workplace.</p><p>Safety tapes are one such method. They’re highly visible and can be used to direct foot traffic, identify tripping hazards, block off areas to control access, and more. NADCO offers three primary types of safety tape, each with its own advantages and applications: anti-slip tapes, barricade tapes, and glow-in-the-dark tapes.</p><p></p>",
            "text_size": "text-base"
          }
        }
      },
