    "custom_img_text_7DYdqX": {
      "type": "custom-img-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_bH4ded": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What Are the Common Applications for Safety Tapes?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_wYfWgH": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>From schools and office buildings to warehouses, distribution centers, construction sites, a variety of industrial facilities, and anywhere environmental conditions can introduce hazards, safety tapes are used for a number of purposes:</p><p></p><ul><li>Color coding</li><li>Marking aisles and boundaries</li><li>Highlighting the path to an exit door</li><li>Blocking access to off-limits areas</li><li>Identification purposes</li><li>Bundling products or materials</li><li>Flagging hidden features, like underground wires</li><li>Directing foot traffic on stairs, walkways, and sidewalks</li><li>Creating physical distance boundaries</li><li>Add traction to a slippery surface</li></ul>",
            "subtext_color": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_bH4ded",
        "text_wYfWgH"
      ],
      "name": "custom image text",
